{
 "kind": "setuhq-stellar-validation-protocol/4",
 "version": 4,
 "frozen": "2026-10-24",
 "seed": 20261024,
 "capabilities": [
  "binaries",
  "rotation",
  "transients"
 ],
 "history": "Protocol v4 covers three capabilities that protocols v1-v3 did not: eclipsing binaries, stellar rotation and transients. It is committed on its own, before any v4 code exists and before any light curve of its targets has been analysed. Targets were drawn from the published catalogues by the seeded rules below, using catalogue metadata only. The results files record this file's sha256 and the commit that added it. v3 (flares, pulsations, CHEOPS) is unchanged and its results stay in stellar_validation.json.",
 "process": [
  "Each capability has a tuning split and a held-out split, both fixed here. Algorithms are developed on synthetic light curves with known answers and on the tuning split only; no held-out light curve is analysed before the validation run.",
  "The validation runs once on the held-out split with the code as committed. A miss is reported as a miss. Any change after the held-out run needs a new protocol version; v4's results stay as recorded.",
  "Counted checks use held-out targets only. Tuning-split numbers are reported and not counted.",
  "A check whose item fails to run counts as not passing.",
  "Planet vetting is out of scope: vet.py, the benchmark and every existing vetting result are unchanged. The eclipsing-binary module's vetting hints are advisory, are not used by any vetting decision, and are not evaluated here; using them in vetting would need its own pre-registered evaluation.",
  "Data: public TESS data from MAST only (SPOC 2-minute light curves, and TESScut cutouts of SPOC full-frame images for supernovae). No CHEOPS data. Cutouts are 11 x 11 pixels, one sector per supernova, deleted after the derived light curves are written; only derived numbers are committed."
 ],
 "status_rule": "validated: every counted check passes; partly validated: more than half pass; otherwise not validated. Always shown with 'k of n checks pass'. Tuning-split results and reported-only numbers are not counted.",
 "binaries": {
  "reference": "Prša et al. 2022, ApJS 258, 16 (TESS Eclipsing Binary stars I, sectors 1-26), VizieR J/ApJS/258/16; the 2-Gaussian model columns (Dp-2g, Wp-2g, Phip-2g, Ds-2g, Ws-2g, Phis-2g), the period and the morphology coefficient (Matijevič et al. 2012: 0 widest detached, 1 ellipsoidal)",
  "selection": "From the 4584 catalogue rows: m_TIC = 1, 0.3 <= Per <= 8 d, Tmag <= 12, Dp-2g and Phip-2g present, 0 <= Morph <= 1 (2707 rows). Split into Morph < 0.5 (1158) and Morph >= 0.5 (1549), each sorted by TIC; numpy default_rng(seed) permutation of each, first 15 of each, interleaved (detached first). The first six (three of each) are the tuning split; the other 24 are held out.",
  "data": "the SPOC 120-s PDCSAP light curve of the first sector the catalogue lists; if it cannot be fetched, the next listed sector; otherwise not run",
