 "rotation": {
  "reference": "Canto Martins et al. 2020, ApJS 250, 20 (rotation periods of TESS objects of interest), VizieR J/ApJS/250/20, table 1 (unambiguous rotation periods)",
  "selection": "From table 1 (131 rows): 0.5 <= Prot <= 12 d and a listed sector (128 rows), sorted by TIC; numpy default_rng(seed + 1) permutation, first 30. The first six are the tuning split; the other 24 are held out.",
  "data": "the SPOC 120-s PDCSAP light curve of the first sector listed, one sector only (no stitching); if it cannot be fetched, not run",
  "limit": "A single TESS sector is about 27 days with a gap in the middle, and SPOC PDC removes some long-term variability, so periods longer than about 13 days are not measured from one sector; the module reports them as beyond its limit. Stitching sectors needs care with sector-to-sector offsets and is not validated here.",
  "targets": [
   {
    "tic": 258777137,
    "sector": 14,
